# nr-relay-media-proxy: wire lines for mixdog-relay (src/media/{mod,proxy,headers}.rs)

No protocol method is added; nothing is registered in a hot file; SERVICE_PENDING loses no name. `pub mod media;` is already in
src/lib.rs.

## native/core/crates/mixdog-relay/Cargo.toml

After the `[[test]]` block of `legs_ingress` (or the last `[[test]]` block present) add:

    [[test]]
    name = "media_proxy"
    path = "tests/media_proxy.rs"
    required-features = ["test-support"]

No dependency is added. The code uses base64 (tests only), bytes, mixdog-js, mixdog-rt, serde_json, tokio (sync: mpsc; macros:
`select!`) and uuid (v4), all listed in [dependencies]; the tests use tempfile and mixdog-rt test-support, in [dev-dependencies].
Cargo.lock and the workspace hack need nothing.

## What nr-relay-server / ingress connects (all in `mixdog_relay::media`)

- Build once per process, after the hub and the unauthorized limiter (the `Arc<Mutex<RateLimiter>>` of 60 per 60 s that the other
  credential-checked routes share) exist: `let media = MediaProxy::start(Arc::clone(&hub), Arc::clone(&unauthorized_limiter), MediaOptions::default())?;`
  It registers the `media-` prefix with `hub.dispatch()`; it fails (`Rejected::Taken`) when another area took the prefix.
- Route: a request whose path starts with `/media/` (`server.mjs`: `url.startsWith('/media/')`) is handed to
  `media.handle_request(request, response).await`, finished with `http1::fail_request("media", ..)` on a panic.
- Nothing is to be done on a leg close or a leg replacement: the hub fails the streams of the leg (`MediaSlot::take_all`).
- The streams of a desktop, the first-frame and idle timeouts, the pause, the cut and the stream limit are the constants
  `MAX_MEDIA_STREAMS` (32), `MEDIA_HEAD_TIMEOUT` and `MEDIA_STALL_TIMEOUT` (30 s), `MEDIA_PAUSE_BUFFER_BYTES` (1 MiB) and
  `MEDIA_KILL_BUFFER_BYTES` (8 MiB); `MediaOptions` exists so a test can shorten them.
- `mediaResponseHeaders` is `mixdog_relay::media::media_response_headers`.
- `lib/media-http.mjs` (mediaResponsePlan, parseRange, mediaEtag) is not ported here: nr-relay-clients-relocate.
